WEBVTT

00:00:00,880 --> 00:00:16,080
I found a local physician willing to provide IV vitamin C infusions. We will begin after

00:00:16,080 --> 00:00:22,600
I can provide them with a dosing and frequency. Can you throw out suggestions so I can get

00:00:22,600 --> 00:00:29,480
started? Well, the physician who's giving you the IV infusions should be making this

00:00:29,480 --> 00:00:34,920
suggestion. I will make you a suggestion, but they're the ones that are that they should

00:00:34,920 --> 00:00:40,920
be the dosing doctors. I will tell you that most clinics that you go to for IV vitamin C

00:00:40,920 --> 00:00:48,760
want to get you up to high doses very quickly. I think it's best to titrate, meaning that

00:00:48,760 --> 00:00:55,040
you started a lower dose and you go up. Now, what dose do you start it? Something like

00:00:55,040 --> 00:01:03,040
20 grams. And then over the course of a month, maybe you're getting up to 60, 80 grams.

00:01:03,040 --> 00:01:06,520
That is also depends on how many times a week you're doing it. If you're just doing it

00:01:06,520 --> 00:01:13,080
once a week, it might take you two months to get up to 80 grams or 75 grams. A lot of clinics

00:01:13,080 --> 00:01:18,680
jump on 50 grams right away and get you up to 100 grams. It could have some side effects

00:01:18,680 --> 00:01:25,240
too. So I don't know that personally, I would do that. I would start at 20 grams. Do that

00:01:25,240 --> 00:01:31,880
multiple times and move up to 40 grams. It also depends on the bags that they're supplier

00:01:31,880 --> 00:01:37,280
that they're getting them from and what increment, gram, increment that they can raise that

00:01:37,280 --> 00:01:42,480
out. So, but I always think it's better to start slower and move up.

